ios,ph,,14139877397,Wed Jun 03 2026 17:21:04 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Poor resolution to a serious food contamination issue,"| love Grab, but I'm extremely disappointed with how my recent complaint was handled. I ordered chicken wings, not realizing the meal already came with rice, so I prepared my own plate and transferred the chicken onto it. While eating, I discovered soemthing inside one of the chicken pieces. Thankfully, I noticed it before | ate it. I pulled it out to inspect, it turned out it was a small cockroach, so immediately took a photo as evidence.
What I don't understand is why my refund request was denied simply because the insect was no longer physically inside the food when I reported it. Of course I removed it to see what it was and to document it. Does that automatically mean the contamination never happened?
It's frustrating to feel like my complaint was dismissed based on that reasoning. Why would anyone intentionally place an insect in their own food just to make a complaint?
Finding an insect in a meal is a serious food safety issue, and I expected it to be treater as such.
As someone who regularly uses Grab, I expected a more reasonable and customer-focused response. This experience has been very disappointing.",dnlobld,,Hi! Kindly send us a PM through FB m.me/GrabPh with your Grab-registered details so we can check this further. Thank you!,Sat Jun 06 2026 05:54:52 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),
