ios,ph,,13797661713,Sat Feb 28 2026 07:39:47 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Harassing me for Grabloan due date when the payment account has funds to pay it - Grab system error,"I have funds in my payment account but Grab is not deducting my loan payment until now. I’ve sent the payment in GrabApp as well so you can deduct it from my account. I’ve been calling your Grab contact center but it is always busy and referred me to a different number which is also not working. 

I have been receiving notifications that my payment is late. You are harrassing me by telling me I don’t pay on time when your system doesn’t deduct the payment from my account. Your system is at fault so don’t even charge me late penalties. 

Please give time to fix it or I’ll report you to the proper government office if you don't stop harassing me. I’ve been trying to resolve this issue because there is NO customer service at all.",Lenaa O.,,"So sorry to hear about this. Please note that on your due date, we’ll automatically try to deduct your installment from your preferred repayment method. If auto-deduction fails (for example, because there isn’t enough balance or the method is temporarily unavailable), we’ll try your other eligible linked payment methods in a set order.

For most customers, we make multiple attempts on the due date and, if there’s still an unpaid amount, we try again on the following days until your installment is paid or your loan is settled. If all attempts fail for that day, we’ll let you know, and you may need to top up or change your repayment method. 

Should you need assistance, please reach out to us here: on FB m.me/GrabPh with your Grab-registered details so we can investigate further. Thank you!
",Mon Mar 02 2026 07:53:01 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),
