ios,ph,,13501163419,Thu Dec 11 2025 13:54:37 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Trip was Cancelled but was still deducted with the amount of the trip from my Gcash account,"On November 21, 2025 at around 8:00 am to 9:00 am I booked a grab car however, since the driver was still far from my location, I cancelled it, however, the amount of the trip was deducted from my Gcash account. I already message the app support but the issue was not resolved. I messaged the social media chat support regarding the issue but they just told me to check the Gcash app timing of refund. But when I check my gcash transaction it was clear that the amount was deducted by Grab. I message their social media support almost every week but then they chose to ignore my message. Now it’s December 11, 2025. No refund was made, even their media support has not responded to my repeated request for update. And according to their policy, it should be refunded within 24 hours, but it has been almost a month now. I hope you will give proper support and answer to the concerns of your consumer/customers, not just auto generated messages. Even your agents were not helpful as they only said to check the wallet’s timing of refund. So grab, kindly, review your support and help sector and improve them before more consumers/customers experience the incident that happened to me",RCSA0418,,"We're so sorry for this booking experience 😔 If no booking was confirmed, unallocated, or canceled, the amount will be automatically refunded and reflected on your account, depending on your bank or e-wallet policy. Posting returned funds normally takes 2-3 up to 30 business days. Don't hesitate to get in touch with your bank or e-wallet provider, as it depends on them the posting process on their charge reversal policy. 

For more details, you may check this link here: https://help.grab.com/passenger/en-ph/360002010168",Mon Dec 15 2025 05:26:18 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),
