ios,ph,,13310893040,Sat Oct 25 2025 06:13:23 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),2,Wasted money and disappointment,"I’ve been a loyal Grab user for quite some time, but recently the experience has been frustrating enough that I feel it needs to be addressed.

First, the app allows orders to stay “in line” even if it takes hours before being accepted by a driver. It’s extremely inconvenient, especially when you’re expecting a reasonable delivery time.

Second—and this is the bigger concern—when an order paid through online payment gets cancelled because it’s been pending for too long, the refund process has been terrible. I’ve had this happen twice, and both times, I never received the refund. Support told me it was already processed, but there was no actual refund on record, even with proof. The next time I reached out, I was told to take it up with the merchant—which shouldn’t be the customer’s burden in the first place.
The support experience has been very passive; the conversations just go in circles without resolution. It’s now been over 30 days, and neither refund issue has been resolved.

I’m sharing this because I genuinely hope Grab addresses these problems. The platform has been great in the past, but issues like these make it hard to stay confident using it.",okam ibasaw,,"So sorry for this booking experience. 😞 If the booking has been canceled, the amount will be automatically refunded and will be reflected on your account, depending on your bank's policy. Please reach out to us via the Help Centre or through social media platforms so we can assist you further with this 🙏️ ",Wed Oct 29 2025 05:46:33 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),
ios,ph,,13310436723,Sat Oct 25 2025 03:09:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Ungrateful company,"I’m a customer of Grab for more than a decade already. Ever since pandemic, we hit the usual requirement for “VIP” status.

However, for some unknown reason they flagged my account as some fraudulent guy saying that I have 8 credit cards in their grab pay.

Among the 8, 4 of those were already deleted from their grab pay way back (!!!) — canceled thru my bank for not waving or the bank just simply closed and the one who took over replaced it. The question however is why do they still have a copy of my deleted cards? Also it is normal to have 4 cards at a time. I have 2 local cards and 2 foreign — wait til you see those mile chuggers enroll their credit cards.

Worse is that ticket is still open til now with no response.

We will never order from grab food ever again. For their other services, there are competitors anyway. We will use grab car only if needed.",X1234567qwerty,,"We are sorry that we did not meet your expectations 😞 Please reach out to us via Help Centre or through our Social Media platforms, so that we can review your concern further and take action. Thank you 🙏️",Wed Oct 29 2025 05:45:01 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),
