ios,ph,,12999444735,Sun Aug 10 2025 15:51:26 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),4,ABSURD!!!!,"This happened on a Saturday night, Auguest 9,2025. 

Grab has repeatedly assigned me drivers who are far from my location—often 10 to 15 minutes away—and many of them still have a passenger to drop off before even heading to my pick-up point. These drivers aren’t even in Cubao, where I’m located. Naturally, I had to cancel several times because the system kept matching me with drivers who were too far away.

I eventually got a ride from a driver who was just 2–3 minutes away and available with no other passengers—proving that nearby drivers are available, but not being prioritized by the app.

Now, I find that I’ve been blocked from ordering GrabFood because of these cancellations—cancellations that were not my fault, but the result of how your system operates. It’s completely unreasonable for passengers to be penalized for cancellations when the system itself is making poor matches. As a long-time user since the pandemic, this experience is unacceptable. I will be deleting my account and will no longer use Grab. This level of service is not something I can support or rely on.",MAEM.,,So sorry for this booking experience 😔️ Our bookings are automatically allocated by the system. The ride you've got could be the only available and the nearest driver in the area. We ask for your patience as we add more drivers on the road to meet the demand. Thank you! ,Sun Aug 17 2025 09:45:24 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),
