ios,ph,,12963259943,Fri Aug 01 2025 14:34:26 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Rip off,"since Grab acquired Uber in Southeast Asia. Without strong competition, Grab had more room to dictate fare structures and route choices, and some users have felt the effects through longer travel times or higher charges.

Thankfully, alternatives like JoyRide, Move It, and even inDrive are emerging and giving commuters more choices—especially for motorcycles and shorter trips. These newer platforms often have:
	•	Lower base fares
	•	More transparent pricing
	•	Driver bidding (in some apps like inDrive)
	•	Less algorithm-based rerouting
#fact",Markypogi10,,,,
