ios,ph,,12376742547,Mon Mar 03 2025 11:06:41 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Consumed by AI makes support horrible,"Reporting ride issues is non-existent. Being forced to talk to a chatbot that doesn’t create a support ticket for me even after meticulously explaining a simple problem that one drop-off point from a multi-drop ride did not happen (which can be viewed from the location history of the ride) is frustrating. In the end, my complaint was never resolved and it might still happen in the future. Your chatbot needs more work and far from barely useful so don’t replace all human support agents.",ChristianJD9,,So sorry for this experience 😞 Allow us to make it up to you. Please reach out to us through our social media channels so we can assist you and take appropriate actions 🙏️ ,Wed Mar 12 2025 14:19:28 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),
ios,ph,,12376319616,Mon Mar 03 2025 08:00:59 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),4,"Convenient, but Can Improve in Some Areas.","Grab is a versatile app that has become a go-to for transportation, food delivery, and various on-demand services across Southeast Asia. Whether you need a ride, want food delivered, or are looking to buy groceries, Grab offers an easy and convenient solution right from your smartphone. The app is user-friendly, and the ability to track drivers or delivery progress in real-time is a standout feature that adds to its reliability.

The ride-hailing service is generally quick, and the drivers are usually friendly and professional. Grab’s food delivery service is efficient, and the wide variety of restaurant options ensures that there’s something for everyone. The payment options are also smooth, with the choice of using GrabPay or cash.

However, the app isn’t without its flaws. Surge pricing can sometimes feel excessive, especially during peak hours, and there are occasional delays in food delivery or ride pickups. While the app’s interface is simple, it can occasionally be a bit glitchy, especially after updates. Additionally, customer service is sometimes slow to resolve issues, which can be frustrating if there are problems with orders or rides.

Overall, Grab is an excellent app for those looking for convenience in their daily life, but there’s room for improvement in terms of pricing transparency and app stability.",Tasinviah,,,,
