ios,ph,,11985961512,Sun Nov 24 2024 10:14:03 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Disappointing,"1. Grab accepts Cash payment but you are not entitled to any points, only Grabpay/Card. This made me switch to Grabpay (higher pts every transaction).
2. Then they require you to subscribe on their Grab Unli plan to be entitled to earn points, regardless if you’re on Grabpay or not. (Not much benefit to customers since minimum transaction is too high to be able to get their shipping discount, and its only Php49).
3. They placed a cash-in yearly limit on accounts which is 100k. I already reached that limit since I use this app quite a lot for transportation. They require you to do verification again. You’ll need to submit an ID and proof of billing for address. I submitted my documents many times but was always rejected due to the ID they want should have an address, as if Passport is not enough as a valid government ID, and the proof of billing I submitted wasn’t sufficient.
4. Takes too long to find a driver even when booking in the city. 
5. Drivers ETA on app is not being followed and drivers take too long to arrive. On the app it says 5minutes ETA, But drivers arrive after 15-20 minutes. Some even cancels the ride after letting you wait that long.
6. Some drivers even click the arrived button already even when they’re still not on the pick up area. Then customers only have 5minutes to get to the ride.

I have been a Grab user for quite a long time now, and what could I say, monopolizing the market could really give you a lot of options on how you can squeeze your customers dry. Guess it’s time to let this app go since there’s already InDrive.",Luffy_9876,,,,
