ios,ph,,10356869213,Mon Sep 11 2023 09:40:01 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Uncaring,"Had the worst experience with Grab today. I ordered food because I had guests over and it was nothing fancy just a simple corndog. I ordered the food around 3:15pm and the eta was about 30 mins so it should have gotten to me around 3:45-4pm according to the app. As I was entertaining my guests, I kept checking the app to see what time it would arrive and my eta kept getting pushed back to the point it got pushed to 4:30pm, what was weird was that my food had already been picked up. I called the driver to ask where he was and why it was taking so long, I was merely told he was “double booked”. Due to this, my guests had to leave and I was left embarrassed as the food I ordered never arrived while my guests were here. I contacted Grab support and they were pretty f****** useless. They were accommodating, but f****** useless. They told me to contact the rider to cancel the order because the food was already picked up or that they would also reimburse me with Php50, which isn’t enough to even cover the delivery fee. The food still arrived but already void of the point of ordering it in the first place because my guests had left. My issue was not resolved by Grab, I am just left alone to either cancel the order or wait for it because I think they did not want anything to do with the issue and just blamed the rider. Don’t set your payment to CC or digital wallet because once you encounter an issue Grab won’t be of any f****** use to you. You’ll just end up frustrated and not enjoying your meal all while Grab just grabs the money and basically tells you to solve it yourself 😂. Guess it’s time to let this app go lol. 

P.S. it isn’t even about the money. I’m just looking for good customer service to help with the issue and I wasn’t able to receive an ounce of help. Top tier useless in resolving issues.",jlao18,,,,
