ios,ph,,10041907971,Sat Jun 17 2023 04:05:56 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Double Booking of Riders is NOT Customer Friendly,"Grab’s double booking of riders which makes customers wait longer than necessary for their food orders is unacceptable.

We pay premium for the convenience and safety of getting our food without leaving the house, but end up getting cold food because of the long wait.

I was told this is to be able to cater to all customers despite the lack of riders.  The solution is to hire more riders, and not to assume your clients will be okay with waiting even if the merchant is proximate to their location",attymlrm,,We group our orders together for efficiency so we can fulfill more of your orders on time. This also allows our delivery partners to earn more by fulfilling at least two orders that are near each other. Apologies if you had an unpleasant experience with this. Kindly send us a message on our Social Media platforms if you need further assistance.,Sun Jun 18 2023 07:33:04 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),
ios,ph,,10040213673,Fri Jun 16 2023 16:01:50 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),2,No riders during rainy season,Grab app has always unreliable during this season. Kinda frustrating that Grab would have to let you wait when in fact there are no available riders in the area.,Irezen,,Apologies for this. It could get a bit harder to book because of the high demand for orders. You may also reach out to us via the Help Centre or through social media platforms so that we can take appropriate action. Thank you 🙏️,Sun Jun 18 2023 07:30:47 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),
ios,ph,,10038813347,Fri Jun 16 2023 07:07:29 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),4,An honest review of a user from a Province wherein Grab does not operate,"Grab is an excellent app–for those who's residing/staying in a place where Grab is available, I may say. That would be for those in the big cities like in the Metro. However, the opposite would be for those who's residing in certain provinces wherein Grab is not operating. The app is not friendly for the latter. You have to go through a lot of clicking, pinning, searching, etc. despite saving certain addresses. Just to be able to book a car for, or have a food delivered to someone who's in a place where Grab operates (e.g. Booking from Masbate City a food delivery from a restaurant in Cebu City to be delivered also to someone in Cebu City) is such a hassle. 

This has been my problem with the Grab app for years. It always takes a lot of patience, and somehow tiring, so I opt to use the other App instead. Even if I would very much prefer to order from Grab if not just for the hassle. Not to discredit the good service Grab has done for me during my stays in Manila, Cebu, Legazpi, but it would be better if they improve this, since Grab has a much broader coverage thus having a lot more options in terms of restos, food stalls, coffee shops, etc., to choose from. 

The world changed so much because of the technology available to us right now, so everything and everyone was brought a lot closer despite the distance. I am glad and thankful that Grab has been an instrument for that, even my convenience and safety during my stays in the Metro and in the big cities. So this is just an honest review from someone who's not permanently residing in those big cities, but has loved ones who do, and would very much loved it if Grab would be a lot easier to access for people like me who wishes to show love in their simplest ways to their loved ones from a distance.",august_augustine,,"Thank you for your feedback. We appreciate you sharing this with us! Rest assured, we are continuously working to improve our services for everyone on the platform. Make sure to look out for updates to utilize our app's features! 💚",Sun Jun 18 2023 07:29:54 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),
