ios,ph,,10011565740,Thu Jun 08 2023 10:04:06 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Zero Stars,"Current issue: Grab has now set up their app to a point where they no longer allow customers to only request for GrabShare. The app will automatically find a GrabCar should it fail to look for GrabShare. You have NO other option out of this except to CANCEL, which will affect your account and flag you if it’s too frequent. I’ve chatted with someone from their support team; she said it’s system generated. In short again, the customer has NO OTHER OPTION. Additionally, another bad part of this is the promo you applied to GrabShare will NOT transfer to GrabCar even if it’s from their monthly Sulit Pack which should have been applicable to BOTH services. Either the developer team deliberately did this to put the customer in a corner and get more money from them or this set up is not what they intended to do. Regardless of what happened, the fact remains that I now cannot rely on Grab because they are pressuring me to use a service I do not want to use. GrabShare is already expensive. You have already raised your rates with GrabCar as well. The very least human thing you could have done is to allow the customer to choose the service they want to use! GRAB IS TOO GREEDY!",Seiu静雨,,"We are sorry that we did not meet your expectations, Rie. Please reach out to us via the Help Centre or our social media platforms so that we can review your concern further and take action. Thank you. 🙏

