ios,ph,,8724842749,Tue May 31 2022 00:13:17 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Choosy drivers,"It is very hard to book rides recently not because there is a scarcity of grab drivers but rather, drivers are choosing their passengers. If grab is a customer-centric app, I suggest that rides are auto-booked on drivers end and cancellation results to fine and penalties. Grab rates are already twice the average taxi fare, I think this and surcharges are enough rewards for the drivers. Because there are no competition (i.e. über) drivers are getting choosy they are turning into taxi drivers.

UPDATE: I don’t think it is because of high demand. I am seeing dozens of cars on the map. Also, when me and my friends book for a ride home they always get rides first - because their fare are higher. In addition, during an ongoing ride. I was about to be dropped-off and I can see my driver scrolling from his grab app searching for passengers looking for a high fares. A workaround to this is I started using the 6seater cars even if I am traveling alone, because their rate is higher and drivers accept higher rates more. Grab needs to do something with their choosy drivers.",Essienere,,"Apologies for this. It could get a bit harder to book because of the high demand for rides. 
Please reach out to us via the Help Centre or our social media platforms so that we can review your concern further and take action. Thank you. 🙏",Mon May 30 2022 07:31:40 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),
