ios,ph,,8261455762,Thu Jan 20 2022 10:16:50 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Refund System,"Happened twice to me already. A driver cancelled a booking but my card was charged already. Grab does not have an automatic refunding system for it. It was days when I found out that I have to file a request to my bank, and it takes weeks to refund.",Fritz Homer,,"We're sorry you had to experience this, Fritz. Since the booking was tagged as 'Cancelled', the amount will be automatically refunded and will reflect on your account depending on your bank's policy. 👍 For any concerns, please reach us via our Help Center or Social Media channels.",Wed Jan 26 2022 07:33:13 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),
ios,ph,,8260674451,Thu Jan 20 2022 04:47:02 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),3,Very comfortable but not at all times.,"Prefer not to use card payment often. Every time you upload a card details (mine is PNB) it costed me ₱50 just to add it. If your order gets cancelled after card payment due to some driver or app reasons, your money will never return back to you, there is no customer service or customer question for you to ask also. Else the app is very useful and comfortable. With cash payment, it is best.",maedhaswi,,"We are sorry that we did not meet your expectations, Maedhaswi. Whenever a card was registered or tried to be added in the app, there will be a charge that will apply, which is used to verify if the card entered is valid. This is what we call Pre-authorization.

Also, if the booking got cancelled, the amount will be automatically refunded and will reflect on your account depending on your bank's policy. You may coordinate with your issuing bank for more information regarding the refund process. 🙂

Since you prefer to use credit card instead of cash, another option for you is to set-up your GrabPay wallet and cash-in via credit card. You can use the balance to pay for your order and ride. Hope this helps! 🙏",Wed Jan 26 2022 07:43:43 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),
