ios,ph,,7299491325,Wed May 05 2021 03:33:08 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Suspended for cancelling multiple grocery orders all drivers wouldn’t even accept,"Now that the covid19 pandemic is ongoing, I rely on Grab to do our groceries. There was a period of almost a month wherein all my family members including me had the virus so we didn’t have a choice but use delivery services like “Grab Pabili”. I noticed that all the riders do not want to accept grocery bookings at all. Whenever I got a rider, they always ask me to cancel my booking and give excuses like “I do not want to wait in line”, “You are listing so many things to buy” & etc. Worse, the app does not have an option to add tips before booking to at least make it more attractive to riders. I am more than willing to pay them extra after all. Sometimes it takes me 2hrs to get a rider kind enough to accept my booking (after I cancel multiple times because they asked me to) but most of the time nobody accepts it at all. One time I came upon a kind rider and he told me that he knows some of these drivers and explained they are just making excuses when they really do not want to get grocery bookings. They prefer restaurant bookings because they are more convenient. After this incident, I noticed I cannot login to my grab account anymore. I finally realized I got suspended. Really? Is this even my fault? What kind of service are you giving to your customers?",defeatedcovid19,,We regret hearing about this. 😔 We strongly advise our delivery-partners to follow and honor the bookings that they have accepted. Please reach out to us via the Help Centre or our social media platforms so that we can review your concern further and take action. Thank you.,Wed Jun 09 2021 08:44:22 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),
ios,ph,,7296421889,Tue May 04 2021 09:44:30 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),4,Suggestion for users’ security,An automatic log out from the app after some inactive time will help protect the Grab user.  Thanks!,WhyMe1104,,,,
