ios,ph,,3738924125,Wed Feb 06 2019 09:23:03 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),5,Just to make the issue clear,"Here is a text message I received from Grab after a few hours that I cancelled my booking:
And here is what I have to say and the truth of the matter:

Hello Grab!
I was not refused a ride. I cancelled the booking because it was not convenient for me to be waiting. Grab car was still far from my location when I checked the location of the same. Taxi was already available in my location hence, the cancelled booking. 

Hi, Grabber.

We are sorry to learn that the driver refused to let you in the vehicle because you are more than six persons.

We encourage our drivers to educate the passenger professionally that we are not allowed to have more than six heads on board if your service type is six seater GrabCar. Overloading is a violation of the Government's policies and traffic rules and regulations, please be aware of that. Instances like these depends on the 
driver's discretion as we know that there are
 penalties for overloading (even if the passengers are kids and/or infants).",ragayana,,,,
