ios,ph,,3629065380,Wed Jan 09 2019 07:00:16 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),2,inaccurate “Driver is nearby” message,"The latest app is displaying “driver is nearby” when the driver is literally “near”. However this is inaccurate because it doesn’t consider the traffic and the path of the driver. Yes, the driver could be near, but it still can take 20 minutes for the driver to arrive at the destination because of restricted streets directions. May i suggest to include in the logic of this message the path of the driver based on waze, better if you could also consider the ETA, like displaying the “driver is nearby” only when ETA is only around 1-2 minutes. It’s very inconvenient that the customer is prepared to go just because the app is displaying “Driver is nearby” but it actually takes 20 minutes for the driver to arrive. Please correct that.",josephru1t,,,,
