ios,ph,,3448931275,Fri Nov 23 2018 00:44:25 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,I miss Uber,"I didn’t want to rate on the App Store for reasons that are not really all that related to the app and the experience of using it, but riding on the bandwagon that is almost all the reviews I have seen thus far.

(1) Ads. I’m paying a huge premium for your almost-always abysmal service and yet I am bombarded with advertisements for almost every click I make on this app. I am pro advertising as a way of earning for developers, but when you’re this big a company that’s supposed to provide instant service as needed to your customers, it gets aggravating how many taps you’re supposed to do before you get to the actual booking part. 

(2) UI. TOO MANY TAPS REQUIRED. Redesigned home page my ——.

(3) Customer Experience. I have, in several occasions sent feedback to Grab about the disappointing service I received from the drivers. I accept that not all will be at the same awesome level that I got used to when I was still using Uber, and acknowledge that there are improvements here and there. But come on! You can do much better than that!

(4) Price. I think I share the same sentiment as with almost everyone in the PH. The prices are ridiculous!!! I need to travel 4.4 km at 11pm. Do not charge me freaking 400php. I miss the days when I can get a 120php ride even during rush hours in the metro. That’s more than 300%!

+ I accept that you’re all into innovations (Grab Pay, Express, etc.) and commend you for that. But man, you can do a better job of listening to what your clientele has to say.",DanaerysTargaryen,,,,
