ios,ph,,3111277353,Sat Aug 25 2018 07:47:17 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),2,Premium is NOT PREMIUM,"Is a 2nd gen Innova a premium vehicle? Is an Innova, manual transmission, with cloth seats, plastic wheel covers, and dirty inside and out a premiuk vehicle? Seriously? What sort of PREMIUM standard do you have? None of the above are premium. Those are regular, ordinary six seater vehicles. Those are what I got when I used your PREMIUM service. What the hell? And I reported this to you yet all you replied was that you’ll inform the driver to clean their vehicle. Does your contact center even understand what I was complainong about? It’s the type of VEHICLE that I was complainong about not the cleanliness. If you dont understand what PREMIUM is, it’s a current generation Innova with leather seats, it’s a Fortuner, it’s a Montero. That’s what would be acceptable but you do NOT deliver on your promise of a PREMIUM vehicle for a PREMIUM PRICE.",Norbert E,,,,
ios,ph,,3108918598,Fri Aug 24 2018 16:54:09 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),2,Bring back Uber,"Prices soared after Uber was gone. They won’t admit it but they took advantage of being the only choice for commuters. Encountered a rude driver too saying not to book grabshare if you have a child. Like why? I’m gonna pay, what seems to be the problem? It’s also very difficult to book specially when you need it most (raining or peak hours). Sometimes, it says no driver available and after giving up, suddenly your driver is there waiting and claming that you have booked the ride. Driver cancelled on us several times too. What an inconvenient when you have been waiting for a while and they decided to cancel when they are nearby. I have a baby with me and we’ve been waiting a while before they decided to cancel. Way to go. Would gladly unistall grab if there is a new booking app in the market.",keyboardmousemonitor,,,,
