ios,ph,,2770150959,Tue Jun 26 2018 00:37:03 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Pathetic,"Drivers are out of control, it takes a while before you could book one only to be cancelled by the driver.",Vhan Jester,,,,
ios,ph,,2765577089,Mon Jun 25 2018 10:24:06 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,"Works OK, but not when needed the most!!","Here in the Philippines, the Grab app decides to not connect to the server properly during super peak situations, i.e. when it's rush hour and raining! It doesn't just say it can't find a driver, the app doesn't connect to the server and becomes unresponsive. You have to swipe up to cancel your booking attempt.

BUT APPARENTLY, THE SERVER STILL SOMEHOW TRIES TO BOOK A DRIVER FOR YOU!

After arriving at my destination, with the app CLOSED and not running in the background, I get a missed call from a driver claiming that Grab booked a ride for me with him. I open the app and the ride is there! I have to immediately cancel to avoid the penalty. What gives? Phantom server instructions? App hanging when you need it the most? For the app itself, ONE STAR. For Grab the service, I'll give them two stars till they shape up. They already have a virtual monopoly on ridesharing here.",DocHarryT,,,,
ios,ph,,2762601532,Mon Jun 25 2018 00:12:55 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),3,I've always loved to use Grab,"Please keep Grab App light, one of the most useful features created was the emergency button, but other than that, we don't need to play Boing Boing game, the locations suggested based on the number of person who booked to were not even recommended in real life. I.e. 2 people booked a ride to Camella Homes - it's a subdivision not a tourist spot or something. So keep it light, I prefer the old app. If you say less clutter, you should mean NO CLUTTER at all. Thank you.",Tfitsshenzy,,,,
