ios,ph,,2660398237,Fri Jun 08 2018 10:09:13 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Unreliable and way too expensive!,"You will most of the give find yourself not getting a ride when you need one. Sometimes, drivers will even ask to cancel the trip. Rates are very high and have no consideration for everyday commuters. In terms of customer service, in the several times I had encounters of double charges or lost items, NOT ONCE WAS I ATTENDED OR RECONTACTED. Unfortunately, it has monopolized the Metro Manila market, so most people don’t have a choice. I hate this app with a passion and so do my colleagues. Once, another car hailing app is launched, will replace grab in a heartbeat.",Bea SJ,,,,
ios,ph,,2652455697,Wed Jun 06 2018 22:21:21 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,"OVERCHARGING, UNPROFESSIONAL DRIVERS","Just using this app because there’s no other choice. I’m sure there are so many other users who think the same way (but just don’t rate the app). I’m in Manila, PH.

I MISS UBER. 

1. OVERCHARGING. It’s ALWAYS ON SURGE even if there’s no traffic, it’s not rush hour, and a lot of cars are available. And the surge is sooo expensive.
2. Drivers are so unprofessional and impolite. AWFUL SERVICE. 
3. CANNOT CHANGE DESTINATION. PLEASE FIX THIS.
4. Grabshare barely gives any savings. What’s the point?
5. There is a lack of drivers/cars on the road which leads to...
6. LONG WAITING TIMES. There is something wrong with the algorithm. The cars I book already have passengers that will be dropped off somewhere that isn’t near my pick up point. My average waiting time before getting picked up is 30 min.",melissa101817,,,,
