ios,ph,,2532510697,Fri May 11 2018 13:20:31 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),1,Inconveniently Inconsistent,"coming from Grab Philippines 
on behalf of the users in Manila, Philippines. The experience with Grab is rather a burden than convenience. Booking is the number one problem. It never works on rush hours. This has been consistent everytime I'm tired from work and I just need a ride home. Grab never fails to disappoint me on telling me that all drivers are busy. I would love to throwback the time where your competitor Uber would give me a ride within 10 minutes max on a rush hour. However, you bought Uber and I expected more from a rich company like you. your second problem is that your drivers would often cancel even if I said I'm willing to wait. they're going to make me wait for 10 minutes and then they'll eventually cancel. this is so frustrating because I wasted 10 minutes for nothing expecting I'd be provided with the service that you offer. Lastly, your prices sky rocket from a normal 200 trip from my house to work to 500 on a rush hour. please look into this as you are our only option now. Since you bought the better ride hailing app called Uber",Manila Commuter,,,,
