ios,ph,,1728900081,Tue Aug 15 2017 14:18:06 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),5,Generally a good alternative to Uber,"Essentially Uber's real competitor. I love their Grab booths and pick up points in major areas, such as the airports. These solve the problems of unclear pickup points (which is usually the case in unfamiliar places), and pesky taxi drivers that keep hustling new arrivals at the airport. 
What I don't like: unlike Uber drivers, Grab drivers know the drop off/ destination before they agree to pick the rider up. In my experience, I seem to get an Uber ride faster than I can get a Grab ride... Because Grab drivers can get a bit selective, choosing riders based on destination. 
But overall, still so much better than the current public transport system in Manila.",Chalcone,,,,
ios,ph,,1727924568,Mon Aug 14 2017 23:46:51 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time),4,Needs more driver vetting and Apple Watch App,"As mentioned in the other comments, some drivers abuse the system by not accepting requests where the destination is ""out of way"". Only GrabCar Premium is responsive to requests, making trips more costly than they should. 

Also as an add-on, please offer an Apple Watch app so we can wait and monitor our requests without pulling out the phone, just as I had done when using Uber. 

Cheers and keep up the good work!
-A",SaiKaze,,,,
